",\"s20\",\"s47\",\"s22\",\"s48\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s49\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"recent\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly describes feeling overwhelmed, stressed, and disheartened by the book swap planning (s3-s5), and disappointed and disengaged by the buying group's lack of dynamic interaction and direction (s20-s22, s47-s49). These are direct negative experiences reported by the user.\",\"variable\":\"negative_aspects\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t4\"},{\"id\":\"fact_711350a85d266f0181213033\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"It appears you're pondering your passion for event planning in your community. Community engagement is valuable, but it's also important to feel motivated and interested in what you're doing. Maybe explore different roles or activities that might reignite your enthusiasm. How does that sound to you?\",\"source_ids\":[\"s40\",\"s13\",\"s39\",\"s32\",\"s58\",\"s12\",\"s30\",\"s57\",\"s31\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{\"event_experience\":1,\"user_interests\":1,\"constraints\":1,\"positive_outcomes\":1,\"negative_aspects\":1},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's history shows a strong interest in community literacy activities (s12-s13, s30-s32, s39-s40, s57-s58) and positive outcomes from well-organized events, but also negative experiences with overly complex planning (s3-s5) and disengaging groups (s20-s22, s47-s49). Option (b) best addresses the user's core passion for community engagement while acknowledging the need for motivation and suggesting exploring different roles, which aligns with the user's demonstrated enjoyment of varied activities like author interviews, reading marathons, and library volunteering, and their caution about complex organizational roles.\",\"variable\":\"response\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,458,\"User: Organizing the book swap seemed like a delightful idea initially, but as I delved into the planning stage, the complexities started to unfold in ways I hadn't anticipated. The thoughts of coordinating different genres, managing people's varying schedules, and ensuring there were enough participants to make it worthwhile all became overwhelming. \",\"user\",[42]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",458,800,\"I found myself trying to devise a system that would work for everyone involved, but with each attempt, I felt more and more stressed rather than excited. The logistics of gathering different books, sorting them by category, and then figuring out how to distribute them fairly seemed like a task that was becoming more daunting by the minute. \",\"user\",[42]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",800,1014,\"Ultimately, it seemed that I was investing too much time and energy into something that was supposed to be a fun community experience, which left me feeling disheartened about pursuing similar events in the future.\",\"user\",[42]],[\"s12\",\"d2\",105,457,\"User: Lastly, I successfully conducted an engaging interview with a well-known author, which led to an exciting community event. The experience of speaking with someone who has had such a profound impact on the literary world was awe-inspiring. I learned so much not only about their writing process but also about their personal journey as an author. \",\"user\",[67]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",457,640,\"It felt like stepping into a world that was both familiar and completely new. Seeing the immediate excitement it generated in the community really made all the preparation worthwhile.\",\"user\",[67]],[\"s20\",\"d3\",107,359,\"User: Lastly, I joined a community-based buying group, but I found it less engaging than I anticipated. Initially, I was excited about the idea of being part of a collective, where people share and collaborate on purchases to benefit from bulk buying. \",\"user\",[138]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",359,728,\"I imagined engaging discussions with like-minded individuals about our shared interests and needs, perhaps even discovering new products or services I had never considered before. However, as time went on, I noticed that the interactions weren't as dynamic or fulfilling as I had hoped; there wasn't much enthusiasm in the conversations, and it felt somewhat stagnant. \",\"user\",[138]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",728,874,\"Additionally, I realized that the group didn't have a clear focus or direction, which contributed to my sense of disengagement and disappointment.\",\"user\",[138]],[\"s30\",\"d4\",105,450,\"User: I even joined a reading marathon for charity! It was a structured event that promoted community involvement, where participants from diverse backgrounds came together to share their love for reading. The organization of the event was meticulous, with schedules, reading lists, and even group discussions planned to enhance our experience. \",\"user\",[63]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",450,761,\"I witnessed how everyone was not just focused on individual achievements, but also on encouraging one another and celebrating our collective progress. It was refreshing to see people's eyes light up when they talked about their favorite books, creating bonds that seemed to transcend the pages we were turning. \",\"user\",[63]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",761,910,\"Ultimately, I found a real sense of community in the challenge, as we all cheered each other on and exchanged thoughts about our literary adventures.\",\"user\",[63]],[\"s39\",\"d5\",107,396,\"User: On a positive note, I started a regular volunteering schedule at the local library. It's been a great way to engage with the community and help out with outreach programs. Every week, I look forward to connecting with people of all ages who share a passion for reading and learning. \",\"user\",[147]],[\"s40\",\"d5\",396,630,\"There’s something special about watching children’s faces light up when they discover a new book or hear a story being read aloud. It’s rewarding to think that I’m playing a small part in fostering a love for literacy in my community.\",\"user\",[147]],[\"s47\",\"d6\",107,342,\"User: I thought being part of a community-based buying group would be a great way to connect with others who share similar interests and values, especially since it promised the potential for bulk discounts on items we frequently use. \",\"user\",[140]],[\"s48\",\"d6\",342,721,\"However, after attending a few meetings, I realized that the dynamics were quite different from what I had imagined, lacking the vibrant exchanges and enthusiastic interactions that I had hoped for. I was particularly looking forward to discussing various products and hearing diverse opinions, as I believed this would enrich my shopping experience and decision-making process. \",\"user\",[140]],[\"s49\",\"d6\",721,1007,\"Instead, the conversations felt a bit mundane and not as engaging as I had anticipated, making me question the value of my membership. As I sat there, I couldn't help but think that perhaps my expectations had been set too high or that this particular group wasn't the right fit for me.\",\"user\",[140]],[\"s57\",\"d7\",105,438,\"User: In fact, I curated a list of must-read books for a community newsletter. It was gratifying to craft something that I hope could inspire and encourage readers all around me. Diving into the world of literature and selecting titles that resonate with different audiences is a unique challenge, but one that is deeply fulfilling. \",\"user\",[19]],[\"s58\",\"d7\",438,707,\"Each book carries its own unique message and has the potential to change perspectives, and I find joy in sharing those insights with others. It provides me a sense of connection with my community, knowing that I might influence someone’s reading journey for the better.\",\"user\",[19]]],\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"public_output_question\":\"I've been involved in planning events for my community lately, but I'm not sure if I should continue with it. What do you think?\",\"public_options\":[\"It seems like you're questioning whether the time commitment aligns with your other responsibilities. Balancing event planning with personal activities can be challenging. It might be worthwhile to evaluate if this is the right time to continue, or if easing back could give you more freedom. What are your thoughts on adjusting your involvement?\",\"It appears you're pondering your passion for event planning in your community. Community engagement is valuable, but it's also important to feel motivated and interested in what you're doing. Maybe explore different roles or activities that might reignite your enthusiasm. How does that sound to you?\",\"It sounds like you might be feeling a bit overwhelmed or finding the process less enjoyable than before. If the structured planning is becoming tedious, perhaps focusing on more spontaneous or informal engagement within the community could be a refreshing change. Consider activities that require less meticulous planning and more personal interaction. How do you feel about trying something like that?\",\"It sounds like you're in a period of reflection about what you enjoy most. Community events can be rewarding and stressful at the same time. Perhaps exploring other interests or roles can provide a sense of fulfillment without the pressure. Do you think trying out different activities might help you decide?\"],\"terminal_expression\":{\"op\":\"var\",\"id\":\"response\"},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"response_audit\",\"audit_instruction\":\"Check actual facts and ALL known scoped counters against original sources. Return audit_verdict=supported only if checked with no unresolved relevant issue; conflict for an established relevant contradiction, or unknown when evidence is insufficient or unresolved. Include sourced corrections/retractions before verdict. Verify the proposed terminal output without silently replacing its option label.\"